  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Laura** (1 review): Part of a loud midway run of older songs, alongside Boing and Awesome Sound, which the attendee loved [5]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Cover It With Gas And Set It On Fire**: back after 56 archived shows (1415 days) [6]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **ween2022-09-17.mk41** (recommended): source not stated; 36 songs; 166 min; rated 5/5 by 3 [1]. Said about its sound: Vocals come through clearly and the low end stays clean, without buzz [4]\n- **ween2022-09-17**: source not stated; 36 songs; 166 min [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Before a stretch of heavy older songs, Gener told the crowd it was time to get brown [5]\n- An attendee says the band played loudly and sounded tight, and seemed to know they were nailing it [5]\n- Setlist leaned heavily on older and rarer songs, with only a few newer ones mixed in, according to a longtime fan [3]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **ween2022-09-17.mk41**: taped by DavidPuddy; transferred by DavidPuddy; source: Schoeps mk41 > nbob actives > baby nbox > Sound Devices Mixpre-6 ii @ 32/48 [1]\n- **ween2022-09-17**: taped by Peter Retzlaff; transferred by Rich Cuiffo; source: Zoom H5 [2]",
